## 5. Distribution of Modified Versions (Patch-Only Rule)

Distribution of Derivative Works—including modified source code, pre-patched files, or modified binaries—is prohibited unless written authorization is granted.

**Permitted Sharing:**

(a) You may distribute modifications solely in the form of Patch Files.
(b) Patch Files must contain only your changes and minimal necessary context.
(c) Patch Files must not include substantial portions of the original Software.
(d) Patch Files clearly reference the original Software and contain a notice stating that the Patch is governed by this License.
(e) Patch Files may not be used to distribute Derivative Works for purposes that would otherwise violate Section 3 (Commercial Use Prohibited).

**Prohibited Sharing:**

(a) Modified source code or source trees.
(b) Pre-patched or modified binaries.
(c) Code fragments extracted from the Software.
(d) Derivative Works embedded in other distributed projects.

