## 6. Forking Restriction (Strict PR-Only Policy)

**6.1 General Prohibition:**
Publicly displaying, hosting, or distributing the Software or Derivative Works (e.g., via a public GitHub "Fork" or mirrored repository) is prohibited, except as permitted in Section 6.2.

**6.2 Contribution Exception:**
You may create a public Fork or copy **solely** for the purpose of developing and submitting contributions (Pull Requests / Merge Requests) to the original Project owned by the Author. Public Forks created under this exception may contain modified code and Patch Files intended solely for contribution review. **Any content in a public Fork must be strictly limited to the minimum necessary to facilitate code review.**

**6.3 Transient Existence (Time Limit):**
A public Fork must be deleted or converted to a private repository within **14 days** after:
(a) The Pull Request is merged, rejected, withdrawn, or closed; or
(b) No new Pull Request activity occurs.
**Failure to delete an expired public Fork constitutes unauthorized distribution under Section 5.**

